# Force LF line endings in the working tree for every text file, regardless of
# each contributor's git `core.autocrlf` setting. The repo stores LF; without
# this, a Windows checkout (autocrlf=true) materializes CRLF, which makes
# `prettier --check` (a required format gate, run in CI) report every file as
# unformatted, and ships shell scripts like scripts/pg-init-multidb.sh with
# CRLF — which breaks them with `bad interpreter` when mounted into a container.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never run EOL normalization or attempt a text diff on these.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
